OL,3,GNEWSATeen 'detached from reality' to
OL,4,Acope with return of aggressive cancer
OL,5,
OL,6,FA teenage boy with lymphoma says he
OL,7,Fcoped with the return of his cancer by
OL,8,Fdetaching himself from his illness,
OL,9,Ffollowing advice from his father who
OL,10,Falso faced the disease.
OL,12,FEthan Griffiths, 14, was diagnosed with
OL,13,FBurkitt lymphoma - a type of
OL,14,Ffast-growing non-Hodgkin lymphoma (nHL)
OL,15,F- in January, undergoing chemotherapy
OL,16,Fand being declared cancer-free in May,
OL,17,Fbefore having an "aggressive" relapse.
OL,19,FThe sport and gaming-mad teen, who
OL,20,Funderwent a new treatment being
OL,21,Ftrialled in Bristol, came home to
OL,22,FMaesteg cancer-free again in September.
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,440,430,260,140,0,100
